# SSG prerender per-page work: `SingleContent.vue`

## (a) Exact sequence of work per `SingleContent` prerender

The 3 composable calls named in the task are not the whole story. The page renders several more `useContentQuery` instances via its children, plus a thundering herd of `useBucketInfo` prefetches. Tracing `import.meta.env.SSR === true`:

**Chained queries (serialized per route via `ssrChains`, `app/src/composables/useContentQuery.ts:27-31, 228-265`).** Each hook callback runs `ssrChains.set(route, queued)` synchronously, then awaits; the next hook's `chainFor(route)` resolves only after the prior one's work completes. So these execute **strictly serially** within one page:

1. **Content by slug** — `useContentQueryWithState`, `SingleContent.vue:97`. Selector `{ type: Content, slug, …publishedNow… }` (no language priority — `languageFilter:false`), `use_index: "content-slug-publishDate-index"`, sort `publishDate desc`, **no `$limit`** → remote cap 500 (`HybridQuery.ts:56,112`). `stripFields: []` (keeps text/fts). `cache:true`, `cacheId = slug`. After docs arrive: `stripDocs` (no-op), `out.value = docs`, `structuralCacheKey` + `writeResponseCache` (ssrCacheStripFields strips `text,fts,ftsTokenCount,_rev`), `readCacheEntry` reads it back from localStorage, `reportCacheEntry`, `reportKeys` (facets + `doc:parentId` per doc).
2. **Translations/siblings** — `useContentQuery`, `SingleContent.vue:293`. Runs after #1 resolves (selector reads `content.value.parentId`). `{ parentId }`, `publishedFilter:false`, `use_index:"content-parentId-publishDate-index"`, sort desc, no limit → 500. `stripFields:["fts","ftsTokenCount","_rev"]`, `cacheStripFields:["text"]`, `cache:true`, `cacheId:"translations:slug"`. Same cache write/read-back/report flow.
3. **Tags** — `useContentQuery`, `SingleContent.vue:373`. Runs after #2. `{ parentId:{$in: parentTags + [parentId]}, parentType: Tag }`, `includeScheduled:false`, **default `use_index:"content-publishDate-index"`** (no parentId-led index!), no sort/limit → 500. Default `stripFields`. `cache:true`, `cacheId:"tags:slug"`.
4. **Related content** — `RelatedContent.vue:26` (rendered under `v-if="content && tags.length"`). `{ parentId:{$in: contentIds} }` where contentIds = `parentTaggedDocs` of the page's tags. sort desc, `limit:50`, default index. `cache` defaults false → no cache write/report.
5. **Read-more tag docs** — `ReadMore.vue:21` (rendered inside RelatedContent). `{ parentId:{$in: tagIds} }`, no sort/limit → 500, default index. `cache:false`.
6. **Copyright** — `CopyrightBanner.vue:11` (rendered unconditionally at page bottom). `{ parentId: copyrightId }` (constant per build) or `{ parentId:{$in:[]} }` when `VITE_COPYRIGHT_ID` unset. `use_index:"content-parentId-publishDate-index"`, sort desc, `limit:1`. `cache:false`.

**Unchained, concurrent `useBucketInfo` prefetches** (`app/src/composables/useBucketInfo.ts:21-31`). Each registers its **own** `onServerPrefetch` posting the identical `{ type:"storage" }` query. Not on `ssrChains`, not reported to `dependencyCapture`, no in-flight dedupe:

7. `useContentHead` → `useBucketInfo` (`seo/contentHead.ts:268`)
8. Hero `LImage` → `useBucketInfo` (`components/images/LImage.vue:35`)
9–24. `ReadMore` renders up to `BATCH_SIZE=8` items (`ReadMore.vue:33`), **two `LImage`s per item** (mobile `sm:hidden` + desktop `hidden sm:block` both render during SSR — `ReadMore.vue:150,168`) → **16** more storage POSTs.
25. `VideoPlayer` → `LImage` → `useBucketInfo` (video pages only; `VideoPlayer.vue:9`).

So a typical article page fires **~6 serial content POSTs + ~18 concurrent identical storage POSTs = ~24 `POST /query` round trips**, all awaited before the page HTML is emitted.

The 18 is an upper-ish estimate, not a fixed count: it assumes the hero `LImage` renders (`SingleContent.vue:754` is behind a `v-if`) and that ReadMore receives a full batch of 8 items. A page with no hero image and 3 related items fires ~7. The order of magnitude — and the fact that every one of them is the same query — is what matters.

Each `useBucketInfo` SSR branch also runs `writeResponseCache(structuralCacheKey(STORAGE_QUERY, STORAGE_CACHE_ID), …)` — `normalizeSelector` + `hashString` + `JSON.stringify(all storage docs)` — **~18 times per page**.

**Per-page non-query work:**
- `mangoCompile(publishedNowConditions)` once (`SingleContent.vue:324`) — template-cached (`warmMangoCaches`), hit after first page.
- `availableTranslations` computed filters translations through that predicate — O(translations), small.
- `mangoIsPublished` builds selector clause arrays per content query.
- `stripDocs` shallow-copies docs and deletes fields (`useContentQuery.ts:42-49`) per query.
- `useContentHead` builds JSON-LD + OG meta via `useHead` (computed, evaluated at render).
- `useReadingProgressTracker` registers a `watch(..., {flush:"post", immediate:true})` (`useReadingProgressTracker.ts:785-813`); at setup `enabled` is false (content unresolved) so it takes the cheap reset branch. May re-fire post-prefetch but `collectSegments` early-returns on null `articleProseRef`.
- `App.vue` setup per page: `usePwaUpdate`, `useAuthWithPrivacyPolicy`, several `watch` with `immediate`, and a `setTimeout(5000)` that later registers a `watch(isConnected, {immediate:true})` → mutates that page's (soon-dead) pinia store. See (c).

## (b) Network calls per page and their nature

- **Endpoint:** every `queryRemote` → `_httpService.post("query", payload)` (`HybridQuery.ts:128`) → `fetch(\`${getUrl()}/query\`, …)` in `HttpReq.post` (`shared/src/api/http.ts:77-93`). `apiUrl` = `import.meta.env.VITE_API_URL` (`globalConfig.ts:12`); `getUrl()` re-runs a regex per call to prefix `https://`.
- **Transport:** native `fetch` (= undici in Node 18+). **No custom agent, no batching, no request dedupe.** undici's global dispatcher pools connections per origin with keep-alive by default, so TCP/TLS reuse happens across the serial/concurrent calls to the same origin — connection setup is not the bottleneck. Per-call overhead is `JSON.stringify(payload)` + fetch + `res.json()` (full body parse).
- **Auth:** anonymous. `customHeaders` (`http.ts:3`) is empty during prerender — `auth.ts` is pulled in only because `useContentQuery` imports `hasPersistedSession` (`useContentQuery.ts:13`), but no `setCustomHeader`/`setProviderIdHeader` runs in the SSR path. No Authorization header.
- **Payload shape:** `{ selector, identifier:"hybridQuery", limit, sort?, use_index?, cms?, includeExpired? }` (`HybridQuery.ts:107-127`). `limit` defaults to `DEFAULT_REMOTE_QUERY_LIMIT=500` when caller omits `$limit`.
- **Per-page total:** ~24 `POST /query` (6 serial content + ~18 concurrent storage), each a separate fetch. With `SSG_CONCURRENCY=1` (default, `vite.config.web.ts:581`), pages run one at a time, so the build pays ~24 round trips × 2000 pages = **~48,000 API requests**, of which ~36,000 are the identical storage query.

## (c) Global / shared mutable state that grows with page count or serializes pages

- **`ssrChains` Map** (`useContentQuery.ts:27`) — **per-route**, so it does *not* serialize pages against each other (the comment at :19-26 is explicit). But it grows by one resolved Promise per route and is **never pruned** — 2000 retained promises. Pages are serialized only by `SSG_CONCURRENCY`, not by this chain.
- **`globalThis.__SSG_DEPS__`** (`vite.config.web.ts:41-58`, `dependencyCapture.ts`): `manifest[route]` grows per route (needed — written to `ssg-deps.json` at end). `cache[route]` is **deleted in `onPageRendered`** (`vite.config.web.ts:668`), good.
- **In-memory `localStorage`** (`ssg/polyfills.ts:24-43`, a `Map`): attributed `hqcache:*` entries are removed per page in `onPageRendered` (`vite.config.web.ts:669-671`), but the **`hqcache:<storage-key>` entry written by `useBucketInfo` is never attributed** (no `reportCacheEntry` call) → never inlined, never removed → one fixed lingering key (negligible memory, but the per-page `writeResponseCache` JSON.stringify of all storage docs × 18 is wasted).
- **`messageCache`** (`i18n.ts:27`) — keyed by language revisions, bounded by #languages. Good.
- **`ssgLanguages`** (`main.web.ts:25`) — fetched once per build. Good.
- **`App.vue` per-page leaks** (`App.vue:72-93`): `setTimeout(5000)` per rendered page; after it fires it registers `watch(isConnected, {immediate:true})` on the **global** `isConnected` ref. `isConnected` never changes during prerender (no socket), so each watch sits idle, but ~2000 watches + 2000 timers accumulate for the build's duration. The immediate callback also pushes an "offlineBanner" notification into each page's about-to-be-discarded pinia store.
- **`usePwaUpdate` module-level** (`usePwaUpdate.ts:27-30`): `setInterval(checkForUpdate, 5000)` + immediate `checkForUpdate()` run for the **entire build**; each tick does `fetch("/version.json")` (relative URL → undici rejects → caught). One interval per process, not per page, but pointless during SSR.
- **`useNetworkSpeedEstimator` module-level** (`useNetworkSpeedEstimator.ts:81-91`): `runProbe(true)` at import + `online`/`visibilitychange` listeners + `watch(userDataSaverEnabled)`. One probe fetch attempt (relative URL, rejected, caught) at startup; listeners persist (once per process — fine).
- **`globalConfig.ts` module watchers** (`globalConfig.ts:121-127,164-173,205-215,412-414,455-474`): `appLanguageIdsAsRef` is reassigned per page by `main.web.ts:53`, firing the deep watchers (`localStorage.setItem("languages",…)`, normalize, synced-normalize) per page — small constant work per page.
- **`userPreferencesAsRef` deep watch** (`globalConfig.ts:412-414`): per-page mutation of the shared ref would persist to localStorage; not mutated during prerender, so dormant.

## (d) Line-referenced hotspots that could be optimized for build time

1. **`useBucketInfo` SSR fetch is unmemoized** — `app/src/composables/useBucketInfo.ts:23-30`. ~18 identical `queryRemote<StorageDto>({type:"storage"})` POSTs per page × 2000 = ~36,000 redundant requests. **Fix:** share one in-flight promise per build (like `ssgLanguages` in `main.web.ts:25`), or at minimum dedupe within a page. Biggest single network win.
2. **`useBucketInfo` SSR `writeResponseCache` is dead** — `useBucketInfo.ts:26-29`. The entry is never attributed via `reportCacheEntry`, so `onPageRendered` never inlines it and never cleans it up; the client can't seed from it on a fresh visit. Pure wasted `JSON.stringify(all storage docs)` × 18/page. **Fix:** drop the write (keep `out.value = docs` for the SSR render).
3. **Copyright query re-fetched per page** — `CopyrightBanner.vue:11-22`. Constant selector per build → 2000 identical POSTs. **Fix:** hoist to a once-per-build fetch (env-driven, like languages).
4. **The serial `ssrChain` forces 6 sequential round trips per page** — `useContentQuery.ts:228-265`. With `SSG_CONCURRENCY=1` (default) the build is one page at a time, each paying 6 serial server round trips before HTML emits. The chain is load-bearing for parent→child dependency (translations/tags read `content.value`), but content/translations/tags could be served from build-time data (see (e)) to collapse the chain to 0 round trips.
5. **Tags / Related / ReadMore use the wrong index** — `SingleContent.vue:373-389` (tags), `RelatedContent.vue:26-30` (related), `ReadMore.vue:21-24` (tag docs). All default to `use_index:"content-publishDate-index"` while filtering on `parentId $in`. Server-side CouchDB scans the publishDate index and filters `parentId` in memory → slower responses → longer serial chain. **Fix:** `use_index:"content-parentId-publishDate-index"` (already allowlisted and used by translations).
6. **Per-slug content query fetches up to 500 docs** — `SingleContent.vue:97-121` passes no `$limit`; slug is unique. **Fix:** `$limit: 1` (the not-found resolver at `SingleContent.vue:217-228` already does this — mirror it).
7. **`readCacheEntry` reads back the just-written localStorage string** — `useContentQuery.ts:258-259`. The string is already in hand before `writeResponseCache`; capturing it directly avoids one `localStorage.getItem` (and a parse-avoidance) per cached query × 3/page.
8. **`ssrChains` never pruned** — `useContentQuery.ts:27`. Minor; delete the entry once the route's HTML is written to bound memory. Note the Map is module-scoped and not exported, so `onPageRendered` in `vite.config.web.ts` can't reach it — this needs a small exported prune helper (e.g. `releaseSsrChain(route)`) rather than a direct delete at the call site.
9. **App.vue 5s-timeout watch leak** — `App.vue:72-93`. Gate the `setTimeout`/watch behind `isMounted` (as the rest of App.vue's interactive chrome already is) to avoid ~2000 leaked watches + dead-store notifications.
10. **`usePwaUpdate` interval runs through the whole build** — `usePwaUpdate.ts:27-30`. Gate on `!import.meta.env.SSR` (and `VITE_ENABLE_UPDATE_PROMPT`).
11. **`structuralCacheKey` recomputed for the constant storage query** — `useBucketInfo.ts:26`. Memoize the key for `STORAGE_QUERY`/`STORAGE_CACHE_ID` (module-level constant) instead of `normalizeSelector`+`hashString` × 18/page. Small but free.
12. **Three comments claim a short-circuit the prerender doesn't have** — `SingleContent.vue:290-292` (translations), `SingleContent.vue:375-376` (tags), `CopyrightBanner.vue:4-9` (copyright). Each justifies its provably-empty `{ $in: [] }` fallback with wording like "HybridQuery short-circuits both the Dexie read and the API supplement" / "before any Dexie read or POST". That holds on the client (`HybridQuery.ts:603-610`) but not on the SSR path, which calls `queryRemote` directly — the exact path those fallbacks exist to protect. **Fix:** land the `isProvablyEmpty` guard in the SSR branch (see (e)) and the comments become true; if the guard is deferred, correct the comments so the next reader doesn't trust them.

## (e) Redundancy vs. data already enumerated at build time

- **`fetchPublicSlugs` already downloads every public Content doc in full.** `vite.config.web.ts:413-441` / `queryDrain.ts:93-101` drains `type:"content"` with `publishDate <= now` via keyset pagination (`QUERY_PAGE_SIZE=500`). The transport returns **whole documents** (including `text`, `fts`, `ftsTokenCount`, `memberOf`, `_rev`, `parentTags`, `parentTaggedDocs`, `parentImageData`, …) — i.e. everything the per-page queries re-fetch. The enumeration result is then **discarded** except for `slug`, `language`, `updatedTimeUtc`, and a `docFacetSnapshot` (`vite.config.web.ts:423-438`, `docFacetSnapshot` at :355-364 keeps only `_id, parentId, parentTags, parentPinned, language`). Every per-page content/translations/tags/related/tag-docs/copyright query then **re-fetches overlapping slices** of that same corpus through the live API. A build-time in-memory content store (keyed by `_id` and `parentId`, indexed by `slug` and `parentTags`) could answer all six chained queries locally and eliminate ~6 serial POSTs/page — the single largest build-time win, especially combined with raising `SSG_CONCURRENCY`.
- **Storage buckets** are fetched ~18×/page with no memoization despite being a public, build-constant dataset — equivalent to `fetchLanguages` which is correctly fetched once (`main.web.ts:25,60`).
- **`useBucketInfo` SSR `writeResponseCache`** is dead data (never inlined) — see (d).2.
- **Provably-empty queries still POST during prerender.** The SSR branch (`useContentQuery.ts:216-271`) has **no `isProvablyEmpty` short-circuit** (that guard exists only in the client `HybridQuery._run` at `HybridQuery.ts:603-610`; `queryRemote` itself has none). So `{ parentId:{$in:[]} }` (translations/tags before content resolves, copyright when `VITE_COPYRIGHT_ID` unset, ReadMore tagDocs when items have no tags, and every 404/redirect page's translations+tags) still hits the API. For ~2000 valid pages this is rare, but for redirect/404 slugs it's 2–3 wasted POSTs each. Three call-site comments assert the opposite — see (d).12.
- **`i18n` messages** are correctly cached per language by revision (`i18n.ts:27-37`) — the ~2k per-route merges collapse to one per language, as the comment notes. Not redundant.
- **`sessionNow`** is frozen once (`sessionNow.ts:24-27`) so `mangoIsPublished` selectors are byte-stable — no per-eval re-keying. Good.

### Summary of per-page prerender cost

| Item | Count/page | Serial? | Avoidable? |
|---|---|---|---|
| Content by slug POST | 1 | chained | yes (build-time store) |
| Translations POST | 1 | chained | yes (build-time store) |
| Tags POST | 1 | chained | yes + fix index hint |
| Related content POST | 1 | chained | yes (build-time store) |
| ReadMore tag-docs POST | 1 | chained | yes + fix index hint |
| Copyright POST | 1 | chained | yes (once per build) |
| Storage buckets POST | ~18 | concurrent | yes (memoize once) |
| `writeResponseCache` (storage, dead) | ~18 | — | remove |
| `structuralCacheKey` (storage) | ~18 | — | memoize key |
| `readCacheEntry` read-back | 3 | — | capture string directly |

The dominant build-time bottlenecks are (1) the ~18 unmemoized storage POSTs/page and (2) the 6-query serial chain per page, both of which re-fetch data that the build-time enumeration already had. Index-hint mismatches on the tags/related/read-more queries add server-side latency to each link in the serial chain.

